# Copy to `.env` and fill in from the Supabase dashboard:
#   Project Settings -> API
#
# WHO ACTUALLY NEEDS THIS FILE: the scripts that read .env when run with no
# `dev`/`prod` argument - `npm run verify:rls`, `check:conn`, `verify:completion`
# and `verify:schema`. Nothing the site serves reads it: every page and every
# server route decides dev-or-prod at runtime from the hostname, out of
# public/supabase-client.js, with no environment variables configured anywhere.
#
# `.env` is gitignored. That is tidiness rather than secrecy for these two values:
# the anon key is public by design and ships in the browser on every page, and RLS
# is the actual security boundary (docs/dev-workflow.md). Keeping them out of the
# repo just means the dev and prod projects can differ per machine after the
# Phase 5 split, without a code change.
#
# The PUBLIC_ prefix is what makes Astro expose a value to the browser. Anything
# without it stays server-side and never reaches the client bundle.

# The URL is always https://<project-ref>.supabase.co, and the ref is visible in
# the dashboard's own address bar: /dashboard/project/<ref>/...
#
# For the key, prefer the `sb_publishable_...` key over the legacy anon JWT.
# Supabase is deprecating the legacy pair, and `publishable` vs `secret` is far
# harder to misread than two near-identical JWTs - which matters, because pasting
# a privileged key here is the one error that would make every check pass while
# proving nothing. Both formats work; verify:rls refuses either privileged one.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_your-key-here

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER put the service_role key in a PUBLIC_ variable, and never in any file
# under public/. It bypasses RLS entirely, so it undoes every policy in the
# Phase 3 migration in one line. Its only home is a server endpoint's
# environment variables, which the project has none of until Phase 6.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
